1:["$","$Ld",null,{"item":{"id":"start-with-two","number":"08","title":"Start with the smallest useful example.","mode":"Generality first","scale":"slide","dek":"Introduce a general model through a small example that preserves its central mechanism. Work through the example before explaining what carries over to the general case.","before":[{"kind":"image","title":"General game · PDF p. 2","image":"/originals/targeting-p02.png","alt":"A simultaneous investment game with n agents, standalone returns, strategic interaction, and a network matrix.","id":"general-game","sourcePage":"2"},{"id":"network-equilibrium","kind":"text","title":"Equilibrium","provenance":"Equilibrium derived from the source model · schematic","formula":"a^*=(I-\\beta g)^{-1}b=\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}(\\beta g)^k b","sourcePage":"2, 10","lines":["\\(b\\): direct incentives · \\(g\\): network · \\(\\beta\\): interaction strength","The \\(k\\)th term is the contribution along \\(k\\) links.","The expansion converges when \\(\\rho(\\beta g)<1\\)."]},{"id":"two-player-calculation","kind":"working","title":"Two-player specialization","provenance":"Worked specialization of the source model · schematic","formula":"\\begin{gathered}b=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\quad g=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\quad\\beta=\\tfrac14\\\\a_A=1+\\tfrac14 a_B,\\quad a_B=1+\\tfrac14a_A\\\\a_A=a_B=1+\\tfrac14+\\tfrac1{16}+\\tfrac1{64}+\\cdots=\\tfrac43\\end{gathered}","sourcePage":"2","lines":["Two players choose investment. Each receives a direct incentive of 1.","One reciprocal link: the other player’s investment raises the best response by \\(\\tfrac14\\)."]}],"after":[{"title":"Each player responds to the other.","kind":"network","stage":1,"lines":["Each player chooses an investment.","An extra unit from the other player raises the best response by \\(\\tfrac14\\)."],"note":"\\(b_A=b_B=1\\) · \\(\\beta=\\tfrac14\\) · One reciprocal link","label":"A TWO-PLAYER NETWORK GAME","alt":"Two reciprocal links between A and B, each with coefficient one quarter. Each direct incentive equals one.","revises":["two-player-calculation"]},{"title":"Repeated responses amplify the initial incentive.","kind":"feedback","formula":"1+\\frac14+\\frac1{16}+\\frac1{64}+\\cdots=\\frac43","note":"\\(a_A=1+\\tfrac14a_B\\), \\(a_B=1+\\tfrac14a_A\\); hence \\(a_A=a_B=\\tfrac43\\).","label":"A TWO-PLAYER NETWORK GAME","alt":"Successive contributions: direct 1, first round 0.25, second 0.0625, third 0.015625. Cumulative responses approach 4/3.","revises":["two-player-calculation","network-equilibrium"]},{"kind":"equation","title":"The general equilibrium adds the same responses.","label":"INVESTMENT WITH SPILLOVERS","formula":"a^*=(I-\\beta g)^{-1}b=\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}(\\beta g)^k b","lines":["\\(b\\): direct incentives · \\(g\\): network · \\(\\beta\\): interaction strength","\\(k=0\\): direct incentives; \\(k=1,2,\\ldots\\): successive responses"],"note":"The expansion converges when \\(\\rho(\\beta g)<1\\).","revises":["network-equilibrium"]}],"diagnosis":"The original presents an n-player payoff and then a general targeting problem. A solved two-player example gives the audience a concrete mechanism to recognize in the matrix notation.","changes":["Solve a small case with the mechanism intact.","Show the contribution of each round.","Carry the interpretation into the general notation."],"preserved":"The source’s payoff and equilibrium condition. The worked example sets \\(b=(1,1)\\), \\(\\beta=1/4\\), and \\(g_{AB}=g_{BA}=1\\), with no self-links.","deferred":"The general targeting problem and eigenvector characterization follow. The expansion uses the source’s spectral-radius condition.","practice":"Find the smallest example in which your main force still operates. Teach it, then say exactly what generalizes.","principle":"Choose detail that carries insight","sourceType":"public","context":"The public research talk supplies the general investment game and uniqueness condition. The compact before calculation and unfolded after calculation specialize that same model to two reciprocally linked players.","beforeCaption":"The source game, followed by its general equilibrium and a constructed two-player calculation.","afterCaption":"A two-player calculation, followed by the general formula.","values":["The compact before calculation and the decomposed after calculation use the same constructed specialization: two reciprocal links, direct incentives 1, interaction strength ¼.","The inverse and infinite-series expressions are derived from the source game; they are not reproduced source slides."],"source":{"authors":"Andrea Galeotti, Benjamin Golub, Sanjeev Goyal","title":"Targeting interventions in networks","date":"2019","url":"https://bengolub.net/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/TIN_slides.pdf","pages":"2, 10"},"topic":"Network games","point":"Choose a simple case in which the main economic force still operates. Work through the relevant choices, interactions, and outcome before presenting the general notation or result. Then explain which features carry over and which depend on the simplification. The example gives listeners a concrete argument to recognize in the more general analysis."}}]
